@prefix cs: <urn:xaas:case-study:> .
@prefix pres: <https://ggen.dev/ns/presentation#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

# cs -> pres bridge: a presentation deck and each of its slides are case-study
# projections, so the case-study never-add-a-claim law (semantic-case-study-pack
# gate 030) and the unestablished-standing law (gate 020) apply to decks
# manufactured by pptx-presentation-pack without either pack changing.
#
# Composition, not redefinition: both vocabularies stay owned by their packs;
# this file adds only subclass axioms. Gates and shapes run with inference
# "none", so instance graphs assert both types explicitly on every deck and
# on every claim-bearing slide (a pres:Slide that renders a claim is also
# typed cs:Projection and carries cs:projectionOf). A slide that renders no
# claim carries cs:noClaimReason instead.
#
# Render edges run both ways, as in the seed: cs:rendersClaim from the
# projection to the claim, cs:renderedBy from the claim to the projection.

pres:Presentation rdfs:subClassOf cs:Projection .
pres:Slide rdfs:subClassOf cs:Projection .
